PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L09U3.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":9,"cefr":"B2b","unit":3,"theme":"Protecting Our Heritage","essential_question":"Whose job is it to protect the past, and how should it be done?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1","title":"Many Houses Have Been Restored: Advanced Passive Forms","objectives":["Students will be able to use the passive in continuous and perfect tenses, with modals and as gerunds.","Students will be able to use prepositional verbs and two-object verbs in the passive.","I can write \"The houses are being restored\" and \"They should have been protected years ago.\"","I can write \"Nobody likes being ignored.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المبني للمجهول في الأزمنة المستمرة والتامة ومع الأفعال الناقصة وفي صيغة المصدر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الأفعال المركبة مع حرف الجر والأفعال ذات المفعولين في المبني للمجهول.","أستطيع أن أكتب The houses are being restored وThey should have been protected years ago.","أستطيع أن أكتب Nobody likes being ignored."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"conservation","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌkɑnsɚˈveɪʃən/","definition":"the protection of buildings, nature or objects from damage","arabic":"الصون / الحفاظ","example":"The conservation of old manuscripts requires special skills.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-W01"},{"word":"renovate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈrɛnəˌveɪt/","definition":"to repair and improve an old building so it is in good condition","arabic":"يجدّد / يرمّم","example":"They renovated the old house and added a modern kitchen.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-W02"},{"word":"authentic","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/əˈθɛntɪk/","definition":"real and original, not a copy","arabic":"أصيل / أصلي","example":"The museum displays authentic tools from the Nabataean period.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-W03"},{"word":"deteriorate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/dɪˈtɪriɚˌeɪt/","definition":"to become worse in condition","arabic":"يتدهور","example":"Without care, the old walls will deteriorate quickly.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"The passive can be used in all tenses. Continuous: be + being + past participle: The houses are being restored. The road was being repaired when we arrived. Perfect: have/has/had + been + past participle: Hundreds of buildings have been surveyed. The roof had been damaged before the storm.\nModal passive: modal + be + past participle: The stone must be cut carefully. For the past: modal + have been + past participle: The houses should have been protected years ago. Passive gerund: being + past participle: Nobody likes being ignored. Perfect passive gerund / participle: having been + past participle: Having been rebuilt with concrete, the house looked strange.\nInformal get-passive: The car got damaged in the storm. Prepositional verbs keep their preposition: People looked after the mosque. → The mosque was looked after. Verbs with two objects usually make the person the subject: They gave the craftsmen a prize. → The craftsmen were given a prize.\ncontinuous: is / was being + past participle • perfect: has / had been + past participle\nmodal: must / should / can be + past participle • past: should have been + past participle\ngerund: being + past participle • having been + past participle\nkeep the preposition: was looked after • person as subject: were given","examples":["The ancient inscriptions are being studied by archaeologists.","More than 300 artifacts have been excavated at the site.","The fort had been abandoned long before it was rediscovered.","Historic buildings must be protected from vandalism.","The old library should have been renovated years ago.","Many craftsmen dislike being rushed.","The tourists were shown the restored rawashin.","The old mosque was looked after by the villagers for centuries."],"common_errors":["✗ The houses are restored now. (in progress) → ✓ The houses are being restored now. (In progress → continuous passive.)","✗ The old walls should have protected. → ✓ The old walls should have been protected. (Modal past passive → have been + past participle.)","✗ Nobody likes ignored. → ✓ Nobody likes being ignored. (Passive gerund → being + past participle.)","✗ The mosque was looked by the villagers. → ✓ The mosque was looked after by the villagers. (Keep the preposition.)"],"arabic":"المبني للمجهول يُستخدم في كل الأزمنة: المستمر (is being restored) والتام (have been surveyed / had been damaged).\nمع الأفعال الناقصة: must be cut، وللماضي: should have been protected.\nالمصدر المبني للمجهول: being ignored، وhaving been rebuilt لحدث سابق.\nنحافظ على حرف الجر في الأفعال المركبة (was looked after)، ومع الأفعال ذات المفعولين يصبح الشخص هو الفاعل غالبًا (were given a prize)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Many Houses Have Been Restored: Advanced Passive Forms”. Let’s learn passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given) together.","on_screen":"GV-L09-U3-LS1 | Many Houses Have Been Restored: Advanced Passive Forms","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Saving Al-Balad”: For centuries, Al-Balad was the heart of Jeddah. Its tall houses, built from coral stone taken from the Red Sea, were designed to keep families cool long before air conditioning was invented. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"For centuries, Al-Balad was the heart of Jeddah. Its tall houses, built from coral stone taken from the Red Sea, were designed to keep families cool long before air conditioning was invented.","visual":"Image GV-L09-U3-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"The passive can be used in all tenses. Continuous: be + being + past participle: The houses are being restored. The road was being repaired when we arrived. Perfect: have/has/had + been + past participle: Hundreds of buildings have been surveyed. The roof had been damaged before the storm. Modal passive: modal + be + past participle: The stone must be cut carefully. For the past: modal + have been + past participle: The houses should have been protected years ago. Passive gerund: being + past participle: Nobody likes being ignored. Perfect passive gerund / participle: having been + past participle: Having been rebuilt with concrete, the house looked strange.","on_screen":"continuous: is / was being + past participle • perfect: has / had been + past participle • modal: must / should / can be + past participle • past: should have been + past participle • gerund: being + past participle • having been + past participle","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The ancient inscriptions are being studied by archaeologists. More than 300 artifacts have been excavated at the site. The fort had been abandoned long before it was rediscovered.","on_screen":"The ancient inscriptions are being studied by archaeologists. / More than 300 artifacts have been excavated at the site. / The fort had been abandoned long before it was rediscovered.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The houses are restored now. (in progress).” That’s not right. We say: “The houses are being restored now.” In progress → continuous passive.","on_screen":"✗ The houses are restored now. (in progress)   ✓ The houses are being restored now.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: \"The house is being restored.\" Is the work finished? … Think! … No – it's in progress. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"The houses are being restored\" and \"They should have been protected years ago.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"The houses are being restored\" and \"They should have been protected years ago.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","المبني للمجهول يُستخدم في كل الأزمنة: المستمر (is being restored) والتام (have been surveyed / had been damaged).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The houses are restored now. (in progress) — الصحيح: The houses are being restored now.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب The houses are being restored وThey should have been protected years ago."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Saving Al-Balad","body":"For centuries, Al-Balad was the heart of Jeddah. Its tall houses, built from coral stone taken from the Red Sea, were designed to keep families cool long before air conditioning was invented. Their famous wooden balconies, called rawashin, allowed breezes to pass through while protecting families' privacy.\nIn the twentieth century, however, many families moved to modern neighborhoods, and the old houses were left empty. Without regular care, wooden beams were damaged by moisture, and some buildings collapsed after heavy rains. Being ignored for so long had a terrible effect on the district.\nThings began to change when Historic Jeddah was added to the UNESCO World Heritage List in 2014. Since then, hundreds of buildings have been surveyed, and many have been carefully restored. Craftsmen who remember the old techniques have been asked to train young workers, because the coral stone must be cut and placed exactly as it was centuries ago.\nRestoration is not simple. Every decision has to be studied: should a damaged roshan be repaired or replaced? Many experts believe that original materials should be kept wherever possible. Having been rebuilt with cheap concrete in the past, some houses now need their walls taken apart and rebuilt in the traditional way.\nToday, visitors can walk through narrow lanes that are being brought back to life. Al-Balad is no longer just a memory; it is a living neighborhood again.","word_count":231,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Look! The old roshan ___ by two craftsmen right now.","options":["is being repaired","is repairing","has repaired","is repaired"],"answer":"is being repaired","explanation":"Continuous passive: is / was being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول المستمر."},{"q":"Since 2014, hundreds of buildings in Al-Balad ___.","options":["are surveying","had surveyed","have been surveyed","have surveyed"],"answer":"have been surveyed","explanation":"Perfect passive: has / had been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول التام."},{"q":"The coral stone ___ carefully, exactly as it was centuries ago.","options":["must be cutting","must cut","must have cut","must be cut"],"answer":"must be cut","explanation":"Modal passive (must be / should have been).","explanation_ar":"المجهول مع الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"These old houses ___ years ago, before they started to collapse.","options":["should been protected","should have been protected","should be protected","should have protected"],"answer":"should have been protected","explanation":"Modal passive (must be / should have been).","explanation_ar":"المجهول مع الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"___ for so long had a terrible effect on the district.","options":["To ignoring","Being ignored","Been ignored","Ignoring"],"answer":"Being ignored","explanation":"Passive gerund (being / having been + past participle).","explanation_ar":"المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"Before the restoration began, many of the district's wooden balconies ______ by decades of moisture and salty sea air.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["have damaging","had damaged","had been damaged","were damaging"],"answer":"had been damaged","explanation":"Perfect passive: has / had been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول التام."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct passive form. Word bank: was looked after, have been found, are being studied","items":[{"q":"The ancient inscriptions ______ (study – now) by a team of experts.","options":[],"answer":"are being studied","explanation":"Continuous passive: is / was being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول المستمر."},{"q":"More than 300 artifacts ______ (find – result now) at the site so far.","options":[],"answer":"have been found","explanation":"Perfect passive: has / had been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول التام."},{"q":"The old mosque ______ (look after – past) by the villagers for centuries.","options":[],"answer":"was looked after","explanation":"Prepositional or two-object verbs in the passive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المركبة وذات المفعولين."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite in the passive.","items":[{"q":"Workers are repairing the old fort.  (continuous passive)","options":[],"answer":"The old fort is being repaired.","explanation":"Continuous passive: is / was being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول المستمر."},{"q":"Someone should have checked the walls before the rains.  (modal passive)","options":[],"answer":"The walls should have been checked before the rains.","explanation":"Modal passive (must be / should have been).","explanation_ar":"المجهول مع الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"They gave the craftsmen a national award.  (two objects)","options":[],"answer":"The craftsmen were given a national award.","explanation":"Prepositional or two-object verbs in the passive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المركبة وذات المفعولين."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Describe heritage work.","items":[{"q":"Describe a building in your city that is being renovated now.","options":[],"answer":"The old market in our town is being renovated.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write about something that has been restored recently.","options":[],"answer":"The old fort in Najran has been restored and opened to visitors.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write about something that should have been protected.","options":[],"answer":"The old mud houses near my grandfather's village should have been protected.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"being + past participle\".","options":[],"answer":"Ancient sites need protection from being damaged by tourists.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence beginning \"Having been…\" about a restored place.","options":[],"answer":"Having been restored, the house now attracts thousands of visitors.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: A restoration report.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences about a heritage site's past using passive forms.","options":[],"answer":"The fort was built in the 18th century. It had been abandoned by the 1950s.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what is being done or has been done.","options":[],"answer":"The walls are being repaired with traditional mud bricks. A small museum has been opened inside.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about what must or should be done next.","options":[],"answer":"The site must be protected from vandalism with better lighting.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin & Speak","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Work in teams of four. Player 1 spins the wheel.","Make a correct sentence about the unit theme using the cue word and passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given).","The team checks the sentence with the grammar box. Correct = 1 point; an extra detail = 1 bonus point.","Pass the spinner clockwise. Play for 6 minutes; the team with most points wins."],"data":[{"label":"is being restored"},{"label":"has been damaged"},{"label":"must be protected"},{"label":"should have been saved"},{"label":"being ignored"},{"label":"having been rebuilt"},{"label":"was believed to have been"},{"label":"not only… but also"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"When we arrived, the main gate ___.","options":["was being painted","was painting","is painted yesterday","has been painting"],"answer":"was being painted","explanation":"Continuous passive: is / was being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول المستمر."},{"q":"By 1980, most of the old houses ___ by their owners.","options":["had abandoned","had been abandoned","were abandoning","have been abandoning"],"answer":"had been abandoned","explanation":"Perfect passive: has / had been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول التام."},{"q":"The rock carvings ___ from vandalism.","options":["must be protecting","must be protected","must have protect","must protect"],"answer":"must be protected","explanation":"Modal passive (must be / should have been).","explanation_ar":"المجهول مع الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"","options":["The old mosque could be saved if people had acted sooner.","The old mosque could have saved if people had acted sooner.","The old mosque could have been save if people had acted sooner.","The old mosque could have been saved if people had acted sooner."],"answer":"The old mosque could have been saved if people had acted sooner.","explanation":"Modal passive (must be / should have been).","explanation_ar":"المجهول مع الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"","options":["The children enjoyed been shown around the museum.","The children enjoyed to be showing around the museum.","The children enjoyed being shown around the museum.","The children enjoyed showing around the museum."],"answer":"The children enjoyed being shown around the museum.","explanation":"Passive gerund (being / having been + past participle).","explanation_ar":"المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"","options":["The volunteers were given special gloves to handle the artifacts.","Special gloves were given the volunteers to handle the artifacts by.","The volunteers were given to special gloves to handle the artifacts.","The volunteers gave special gloves to handle the artifacts."],"answer":"The volunteers were given special gloves to handle the artifacts.","explanation":"Prepositional or two-object verbs in the passive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المركبة وذات المفعولين."},{"q":"My bike ___ damaged when the wall collapsed.","options":["has got be","was getting been","became being","got"],"answer":"got","explanation":"Prepositional or two-object verbs in the passive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المركبة وذات المفعولين."},{"q":"Since the excavation began in 2004, more than ten thousand artifacts ______ at the site, including coins, jewelry and pottery.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["have been discovered","have discovered","had discovered","are discovering"],"answer":"have been discovered","explanation":"Perfect passive: has / had been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول التام."},{"q":"______ for centuries under desert sand, the ancient city of Hegra was remarkably well preserved when archaeologists began excavating it.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["Burying","Having buried","Having been buried","Been buried"],"answer":"Having been buried","explanation":"Passive gerund (being / having been + past participle).","explanation_ar":"المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"\"The house is being restored.\" What does this mean?","options":["The house will be restored next year.","The restoration is finished.","Work on the house is in progress now.","Nobody is working on the house."],"answer":"Work on the house is in progress now.","explanation":"Continuous passive: is / was being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول المستمر."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Historic Jeddah (Al-Balad): tall coral-stone houses with dark wooden balconies (rawashin); scaffolding on one house where craftsmen are repairing a carved wooden window; an old craftsman teaching young workers; tourists walking through a narrow lane. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Historic Jeddah (Al-Balad): tall coral-stone houses with dark wooden balconies (rawashin); scaffolding on one house where craftsmen are repairing a carved wooden window; an old craftsman teaching young workers; tourists walking through a narrow lane"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged)"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows conservation (the protection of buildings, nature or objects from damage); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing conservation: the protection of buildings, nature or objects from damage"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows renovate (to repair and improve an old building so it is in good condition); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing renovate: to repair and improve an old building so it is in good condition"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows authentic (real and original, not a copy); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing authentic: real and original, not a copy"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows deteriorate (to become worse in condition); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing deteriorate: to become worse in condition"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin & Speak”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin & Speak"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-W01","script":"conservation. conservation. The conservation of old manuscripts requires special skills.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-W02","script":"renovate. renovate. They renovated the old house and added a modern kitchen.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-W03","script":"authentic. authentic. The museum displays authentic tools from the Nabataean period.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-W04","script":"deteriorate. deteriorate. Without care, the old walls will deteriorate quickly.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-T1","script":"For centuries, Al-Balad was the heart of Jeddah. Its tall houses, built from coral stone taken from the Red Sea, were designed to keep families cool long before air conditioning was invented. Their famous wooden balconies, called rawashin, allowed breezes to pass through while protecting families' privacy. In the twentieth century, however, many families moved to modern neighborhoods, and the old houses were left empty. Without regular care, wooden beams were damaged by moisture, and some buildings collapsed after heavy rains. Being ignored for so long had a terrible effect on the district. Things began to change when Historic Jeddah was added to the UNESCO World Heritage List in 2014. Since then, hundreds of buildings have been surveyed, and many have been carefully restored. Craftsmen who remember the old techniques have been asked to train young workers, because the coral stone must be cut and placed exactly as it was centuries ago. Restoration is not simple. Every decision has to be studied: should a damaged roshan be repaired or replaced? Many experts believe that original materials should be kept wherever possible. Having been rebuilt with cheap concrete in the past, some houses now need their walls taken apart and rebuilt in the traditional way. Today, visitors can walk through narrow lanes that are being brought back to life. Al-Balad is no longer just a memory; it is a living neighborhood again.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Many Houses Have Been Restored: Advanced Passive Forms”. Let’s learn passive in continuous and perfect tenses (is being restored, has been restored, had been damaged); modal passives (must be protected, should have been saved); passive gerunds (being ignored, having been rebuilt); get-passive (got damaged); prepositional verbs in the passive (was looked after); verbs with two objects (were given) together. Listen to the start of “Saving Al-Balad”: For centuries, Al-Balad was the heart of Jeddah. Its tall houses, built from coral stone taken from the Red Sea, were designed to keep families cool long before air conditioning was invented. Look at the green words. The passive can be used in all tenses. Continuous: be + being + past participle: The houses are being restored. The road was being repaired when we arrived. Perfect: have/has/had + been + past participle: Hundreds of buildings have been surveyed. The roof had been damaged before the storm. Modal passive: modal + be + past participle: The stone must be cut carefully. For the past: modal + have been + past participle: The houses should have been protected years ago. Passive gerund: being + past participle: Nobody likes being ignored. Perfect passive gerund / participle: having been + past participle: Having been rebuilt with concrete, the house looked strange. Here are some examples. The ancient inscriptions are being studied by archaeologists. More than 300 artifacts have been excavated at the site. The fort had been abandoned long before it was rediscovered. Be careful! Some learners say: “The houses are restored now. (in progress).” That’s not right. We say: “The houses are being restored now.” In progress → continuous passive. Quick check: \"The house is being restored.\" Is the work finished? … Think! … No – it's in progress. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"The houses are being restored\" and \"They should have been protected years ago.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2","title":"It Was Once Believed That…: Passive Reporting Structures About the Past","objectives":["Students will be able to report past beliefs and claims with It was believed that… and X was thought to…","Students will be able to report present opinions about past events with X is thought to have been + past participle.","I can write \"It was once believed that the city was built by giants.\"","I can write \"The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من نقل المعتقدات والادعاءات الماضية بـ It was believed that… وX was thought to…","سيتمكن الطلاب من نقل آراء حالية عن أحداث ماضية بـ X is thought to have been + التصريف الثالث.","أستطيع أن أكتب It was once believed that the city was built by giants.","أستطيع أن أكتب The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"artifact","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɑrtəˌfækt/","definition":"an object made by people long ago that has historical interest","arabic":"قطعة أثرية","example":"Archaeologists found pottery and other artifacts at the site.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS2-W01"},{"word":"excavate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈɛkskəˌveɪt/","definition":"to dig carefully to find old objects or buildings","arabic":"ينقّب","example":"The team excavated an ancient settlement near Al-Ula.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS2-W02"},{"word":"archaeologist","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɑrkiˈɑlədʒɪst/","definition":"a person who studies the past by digging up old objects and buildings","arabic":"عالِم آثار","example":"The archaeologist cleaned the coin with a soft brush.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS2-W03"},{"word":"landmark","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlændˌmɑrk/","definition":"a famous building or place that is easy to recognize","arabic":"معلَم","example":"The Kingdom Centre is a famous Riyadh landmark.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"When we report what people believed in the past, the reporting verb is in the past: It was believed that the Earth was flat. The ancient city was thought to be a myth. Use to have + past participle for something even earlier: In 1900, the inscriptions were believed to have been carved by travelers.\nWhen we report what people think now about the past, the reporting verb is in the present and the infinitive is perfect: The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s. (People think now; the building happened in the past.) The manuscripts are believed to have been hidden in a cave. Use to have been + past participle when the subject received the action.\nOther useful forms: It has been suggested that… (a recent idea), It has long been known that…, X is known to have been… (a fact accepted by experts). Choose carefully: is said to have built (the subject built something) vs is said to have been built (the subject was built).\npast belief: It was believed that… / X was believed to be…\npresent belief about the past: X is thought to have been + past participle\nactive vs passive infinitive: to have built ≠ to have been built\nIt has been suggested that… • It has long been known that…","examples":["It was once believed that Hegra was built by giants.","The inscriptions are thought to have been carved around 500 BCE.","The ancient road is known to have been used by incense traders.","It was widely thought that the manuscripts had been destroyed.","The old well is said to have been dug by the founder of the village.","It has been suggested that the site was a market as well as a temple.","The coins were believed to have come from Yemen.","The city is believed to have had more than ten thousand inhabitants."],"common_errors":["✗ The fort is thought to have built in the 1700s. → ✓ The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s. (The fort received the action → passive.)","✗ It was believing that the Earth was flat. → ✓ It was believed that the Earth was flat. (Passive → was + past participle.)","✗ The manuscripts are believed that they were hidden. → ✓ The manuscripts are believed to have been hidden. (Don't mix the two patterns.)","✗ The well is said to be dug 300 years ago. → ✓ The well is said to have been dug 300 years ago. (Past action → to have been + past participle.)"],"arabic":"لنقل معتقدات الماضي: It was believed that the Earth was flat. / The city was thought to be a myth.\nلنقل ما يعتقده الناس الآن عن الماضي: The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s.\nانتبه: is said to have built (الفاعل بنى) تختلف عن is said to have been built (الفاعل بُني).\nIt has been suggested that… لفكرة حديثة، وIt has long been known that… لحقيقة معروفة منذ زمن."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It Was Once Believed That…: Passive Reporting Structures About the Past”. Let’s learn passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… together.","on_screen":"GV-L09-U3-LS2 | It Was Once Believed That…: Passive Reporting Structures About the Past","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: The palace is thought to have been built around 1800. The site was not believed to be important until 1970. Is the well believed to have been dug by hand?","on_screen":"The palace is thought to have been built around 1800. | The site was not believed to be important until 1970. | Is the well believed to have been dug by hand?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"When we report what people believed in the past, the reporting verb is in the past: It was believed that the Earth was flat. The ancient city was thought to be a myth. Use to have + past participle for something even earlier: In 1900, the inscriptions were believed to have been carved by travelers. When we report what people think now about the past, the reporting verb is in the present and the infinitive is perfect: The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s. (People think now; the building happened in the past.) The manuscripts are believed to have been hidden in a cave. Use to have been + past participle when the subject received the action.","on_screen":"past belief: It was believed that… / X was believed to be… • present belief about the past: X is thought to have been + past participle • active vs passive infinitive: to have built ≠ to have been built","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It was once believed that Hegra was built by giants. The inscriptions are thought to have been carved around 500 BCE. The ancient road is known to have been used by incense traders.","on_screen":"It was once believed that Hegra was built by giants. / The inscriptions are thought to have been carved around 500 BCE. / The ancient road is known to have been used by incense traders.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The fort is thought to have built in the 1700s.” That’s not right. We say: “The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s.” The fort received the action → passive.","on_screen":"✗ The fort is thought to have built in the 1700s.   ✓ The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: \"The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s.\" When do people think this? When was it built? … Think! … People think it now; it was built in the past. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"It was once believed that the city was built by giants.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"It was once believed that the city was built by giants.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been….","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","لنقل معتقدات الماضي: It was believed that the Earth was flat. / The city was thought to be a myth.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The fort is thought to have built in the 1700s. — الصحيح: The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب It was once believed that the city was built by giants."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___ that the ancient city of Hegra was built by giants.","options":["It was once believing","They were once believed","It was once believed","It once believed"],"answer":"It was once believed","explanation":"It was believed / thought / said that… (past belief).","explanation_ar":"It was believed that."},{"q":"The old fort is thought ___ in the 1700s.","options":["being built","to build","to have built","to have been built"],"answer":"to have been built","explanation":"Subject + is thought + to have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"In the 1800s, the inscriptions ___ to be meaningless.","options":["thought","were thinking","were thought","had thought them"],"answer":"were thought","explanation":"Subject + was believed / thought + to… (past belief).","explanation_ar":"الفاعل + was believed to."},{"q":"The king is said ___ the fort to protect the oasis.","options":["to have built","building","to have been built","to be built"],"answer":"to have built","explanation":"Active (to have done) or passive (to have been done)?","explanation_ar":"المعلوم أم المجهول؟"},{"q":"","options":["The manuscripts believe to have been hidden in a cave.","The manuscripts are believed to have been hidden in a cave.","The manuscripts are believed that they were hidden in a cave.","The manuscripts are believing to have been hidden in a cave."],"answer":"The manuscripts are believed to have been hidden in a cave.","explanation":"Don't mix the two patterns.","explanation_ar":"لا خلط بين النمطين."},{"q":"The ancient incense road that passed through the Arabian Peninsula ______ by traders carrying frankincense from Yemen to the Mediterranean.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["is known to have been used","is known to have used","is knowing to be used","knows to have been used"],"answer":"is known to have been used","explanation":"Subject + is thought + to have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"to have been done."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct form. Word bank: was widely believed, to have been dug, to have had","items":[{"q":"The old well is said ______ (dig) by the founder of the village.","options":[],"answer":"to have been dug","explanation":"Subject + is thought + to have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"It ______ (widely / believe) that the manuscripts had been destroyed.","options":[],"answer":"was widely believed","explanation":"It was believed / thought / said that… (past belief).","explanation_ar":"It was believed that."},{"q":"The ancient city is believed ______ (have) ten thousand inhabitants.","options":[],"answer":"to have had","explanation":"Active (to have done) or passive (to have been done)?","explanation_ar":"المعلوم أم المجهول؟"}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with a passive reporting structure.","items":[{"q":"People believe that traders carved these inscriptions. (These inscriptions…)  (to have been)","options":[],"answer":"These inscriptions are believed to have been carved by traders.","explanation":"Subject + is thought + to have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"In the past, people thought that the site was a cemetery. (It…)  (It was thought)","options":[],"answer":"It was thought that the site was a cemetery.","explanation":"It was believed / thought / said that… (past belief).","explanation_ar":"It was believed that."},{"q":"Experts say that the mosque was rebuilt in 1850. (The mosque…)  (is said to have been)","options":[],"answer":"The mosque is said to have been rebuilt in 1850.","explanation":"Subject + is thought + to have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"to have been done."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Report beliefs about the past.","items":[{"q":"Write about something people once believed that turned out to be false.","options":[],"answer":"It was once believed that the Sun moved around the Earth.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write about a building in your region with \"is thought to have been built\".","options":[],"answer":"The old fort in Taif is thought to have been built in the 19th century.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"is known to have been used\".","options":[],"answer":"This old road is known to have been used by pilgrims.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"It has been suggested that…\".","options":[],"answer":"It has been suggested that the old market should become a museum.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence contrasting \"said to have built\" and \"said to have been built\".","options":[],"answer":"The merchant is said to have built the house. The house is said to have been built in 1890.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Museum label.","items":[{"q":"Write a museum label for an artifact using two passive reporting structures.","options":[],"answer":"This bronze lamp is believed to have been made in the 2nd century. It is thought to have been used in a temple.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence about what people believed about the artifact in the past.","options":[],"answer":"When it was found, it was believed to be a cooking pot.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence about how the artifact is being protected now.","options":[],"answer":"It is being kept in a glass case at a controlled temperature.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Tic-Tac-Grammar","mechanic":"tic_tac_toe","rules":["Two teams: X and O. Team X chooses a square.","Using the cue, the team says a correct sentence with passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… (the form in brackets: +, – or ?).","If the class and teacher agree it is correct, the team marks the square.","Three squares in a row wins. Play a second round with the grid turned around."],"data":[{"cue":"the old fort / restore / now (is being)"},{"cue":"many houses / damage / by rain (have been)"},{"cue":"heritage sites / protect (must be)"},{"cue":"the mosque / repair / years ago (should have been)"},{"cue":"nobody / like / ignore (being)"},{"cue":"rebuild / with concrete / the house / look modern (having been)"},{"cue":"the city / believe / be founded / in the 7th century (was believed to have been)"},{"cue":"the manuscripts / think / lose (were thought to have been)"},{"cue":"the project / both / protect / old houses / and / create jobs"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___ that the inscriptions were written in an unknown language.","options":["It once thought","It was once thought","They were once thought","It was once thinking"],"answer":"It was once thought","explanation":"It was believed / thought / said that… (past belief).","explanation_ar":"It was believed that."},{"q":"The ancient coins are believed ___ from Yemen.","options":["to have come","to come yesterday","coming","to have been come"],"answer":"to have come","explanation":"Active (to have done) or passive (to have been done)?","explanation_ar":"المعلوم أم المجهول؟"},{"q":"The palace is thought ___ in only three years.","options":["to complete","to have completed","completing","to have been completed"],"answer":"to have been completed","explanation":"Subject + is thought + to have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"Until 1970, the site ___ to be unimportant.","options":["considered","was considered","was considering","had considered it"],"answer":"was considered","explanation":"Subject + was believed / thought + to… (past belief).","explanation_ar":"الفاعل + was believed to."},{"q":"","options":["The bridge is said to have been designed by a famous engineer.","The bridge is said that it was designed by a famous engineer.","The bridge says to have been designed by a famous engineer.","The bridge is said to have designed by a famous engineer."],"answer":"The bridge is said to have been designed by a famous engineer.","explanation":"Don't mix the two patterns.","explanation_ar":"لا خلط بين النمطين."},{"q":"The merchant is said ___ the mosque for the whole village.","options":["building it","to have been built","to be built","to have built"],"answer":"to have built","explanation":"Active (to have done) or passive (to have been done)?","explanation_ar":"المعلوم أم المجهول؟"},{"q":"","options":["It suggested been that the site was used as a market.","It has been suggested that the site was used as a market.","It has been suggesting that the site was used as a market.","It has suggested that the site was used as a market."],"answer":"It has been suggested that the site was used as a market.","explanation":"It was believed / thought / said that… (past belief).","explanation_ar":"It was believed that."},{"q":"The ruins near Tayma ______ part of one of the oldest settlements in the Arabian Peninsula, dating back thousands of years.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["are believing to be","believe to have been","are believed to have","are believed to have been"],"answer":"are believed to have been","explanation":"Subject + is thought + to have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"For many years, the dinosaur bones found in the desert ______ to be the remains of a giant camel.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["had thought","thought","were thought","were thinking"],"answer":"were thought","explanation":"Subject + was believed / thought + to… (past belief).","explanation_ar":"الفاعل + was believed to."},{"q":"\"The fort is thought to have been built in 1790.\" What does \"is thought\" refer to?","options":["what people thought in 1790","a future plan","what people think now","what the fort thinks"],"answer":"what people think now","explanation":"Subject + is thought + to have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"to have been done."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"An archaeology lab: an archaeologist examining an ancient inscription under a magnifying lamp, a timeline on the wall showing \"once believed\" vs \"now known\", old maps and pottery fragments on a table. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"An archaeology lab: an archaeologist examining an ancient inscription under a magnifying lamp, a timeline on the wall showing \"once believed\" vs \"now known\", old maps and pottery fragments on a table"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been…: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Protecting Our Heritage”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows artifact (an object made by people long ago that has historical interest); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing artifact: an object made by people long ago that has historical interest"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows excavate (to dig carefully to find old objects or buildings); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing excavate: to dig carefully to find old objects or buildings"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows archaeologist (a person who studies the past by digging up old objects and buildings); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing archaeologist: a person who studies the past by digging up old objects and buildings"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows landmark (a famous building or place that is easy to recognize); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing landmark: a famous building or place that is easy to recognize"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Tic-Tac-Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Tic-Tac-Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS2-W01","script":"artifact. artifact. Archaeologists found pottery and other artifacts at the site.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS2-W02","script":"excavate. excavate. The team excavated an ancient settlement near Al-Ula.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS2-W03","script":"archaeologist. archaeologist. The archaeologist cleaned the coin with a soft brush.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS2-W04","script":"landmark. landmark. The Kingdom Centre is a famous Riyadh landmark.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It Was Once Believed That…: Passive Reporting Structures About the Past”. Let’s learn passive reporting structures for past events and beliefs: It was believed / thought / said that…; X was believed to be / to have been…; X is thought to have been built (present report about the past); It has been suggested that…; X is known to have been… together. Remember these patterns: The palace is thought to have been built around 1800. The site was not believed to be important until 1970. Is the well believed to have been dug by hand? When we report what people believed in the past, the reporting verb is in the past: It was believed that the Earth was flat. The ancient city was thought to be a myth. Use to have + past participle for something even earlier: In 1900, the inscriptions were believed to have been carved by travelers. When we report what people think now about the past, the reporting verb is in the present and the infinitive is perfect: The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s. (People think now; the building happened in the past.) The manuscripts are believed to have been hidden in a cave. Use to have been + past participle when the subject received the action. Here are some examples. It was once believed that Hegra was built by giants. The inscriptions are thought to have been carved around 500 BCE. The ancient road is known to have been used by incense traders. Be careful! Some learners say: “The fort is thought to have built in the 1700s.” That’s not right. We say: “The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s.” The fort received the action → passive. Quick check: \"The fort is thought to have been built in the 1700s.\" When do people think this? When was it built? … Think! … People think it now; it was built in the past. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"It was once believed that the city was built by giants.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3","title":"Restore, Renovate or Preserve? Conservation Vocabulary and Context Clues","objectives":["Students will be able to use conservation vocabulary precisely, choosing between words with related meanings.","Students will be able to use context clues to determine the meaning of unfamiliar heritage words.","I can explain the difference between \"restore\" and \"renovate\".","I can work out the meaning of \"dilapidated\" from the sentence around it."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام مفردات الحفاظ على التراث بدقة واختيار الكلمة المناسبة بين الكلمات المتقاربة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام قرائن السياق لتحديد معنى كلمات التراث غير المألوفة.","أستطيع أن أشرح الفرق بين restore وrenovate.","أستطيع أن أستنتج معنى dilapidated من الجملة المحيطة بها."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"craftsmanship","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkræftsmənˌʃɪp/","definition":"the skill with which something is made by hand","arabic":"الإتقان الحِرفي","example":"The doors show amazing craftsmanship.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W01"},{"word":"legacy","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɛɡəsi/","definition":"something important that people from the past leave for the future","arabic":"إرث","example":"The old mosques are part of our grandparents' legacy.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W02"},{"word":"vandalism","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvændəlɪzəm/","definition":"the crime of deliberately damaging public or private property","arabic":"التخريب","example":"Vandalism has damaged several ancient rock carvings.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W03"},{"word":"intangible","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈtændʒəbəl/","definition":"not physical; something you can't touch, such as traditions and songs","arabic":"غير مادي","example":"Arabic calligraphy is part of the world's intangible cultural heritage.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W04"},{"word":"dilapidated","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/dəˈlæpəˌdeɪtɪd/","definition":"old and in very bad condition","arabic":"متهالك / متداعٍ","example":"The dilapidated house was finally restored.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W05"},{"word":"inscription","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈskrɪpʃən/","definition":"words cut into stone or metal","arabic":"نقش","example":"Ancient inscriptions were found on the rocks near Tayma.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W06"},{"word":"safeguard","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈseɪfˌɡɑrd/","definition":"to protect something from harm or loss","arabic":"يصون / يحمي","example":"New laws safeguard historic buildings.","image_id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W07","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W07"}],"explanation":{"text":"Words with related meanings: preserve = keep something as it is, stop it from changing; conserve = protect it carefully, especially from damage or decay; restore = return it to its original condition; renovate = repair and improve it, often with modern features; rebuild = build it again after it was destroyed. An authentic object is original; a replica is an exact copy.\nHeritage words: artifact (an old object made by people), inscription (words cut into stone), archaeologist / excavate (study the past by digging), landmark (a famous, recognizable place), craftsmanship (skill in making things by hand), legacy (what the past leaves us), intangible heritage (traditions, songs, skills – things you can't touch), vandalism (deliberate damage).\nContext clues help with difficult words. Definition: \"The house was dilapidated—old, broken and falling apart.\" Example: \"Intangible heritage, such as folk songs and traditional dances, …\" Contrast: \"Unlike the authentic coins, the copies were made of plastic.\" Inference (from the situation): \"The dilapidated walls had to be held up with wooden beams.\"\nCollocations/phrases: preserve: keep it as it is • conserve: protect it from damage | restore: bring back its original condition • renovate: repair and modernize | rebuild: build again • excavate: dig up carefully • safeguard: protect from loss","examples":["The museum works to preserve the manuscripts in a dark, cool room.","The palace was restored using the original materials.","The old house was renovated and turned into a modern café.","The authentic doors were replaced with replicas in the 1990s.","Archaeologists excavated a settlement that is 3,000 years old.","Vandalism has damaged several ancient rock carvings.","Traditional storytelling is part of our intangible heritage.","The fine carving on the doors shows incredible craftsmanship."],"common_errors":["✗ They renovated the old palace exactly as it was in 1850. → ✓ They restored the old palace exactly as it was in 1850. (Original condition → restore.)","✗ The museum restored the old manuscripts by keeping them in the dark. → ✓ The museum preserved the old manuscripts by keeping them in the dark. (Keep as it is → preserve.)","✗ These are authentic copies of the coins. → ✓ These are replicas of the coins. (A copy is not authentic.)","✗ The archaeologists dug the artifacts quickly with machines. → ✓ The archaeologists excavated the artifacts carefully by hand. (Excavation is slow and careful.)"],"arabic":"كلمات متقاربة: preserve (يحفظ كما هو)، conserve (يصون من التلف)، restore (يعيده إلى حالته الأصلية)، renovate (يجدّد ويحدّث)، rebuild (يعيد بناءه بعد تهدّمه).\nauthentic (أصلي) ≠ replica (نسخة مطابقة)، وintangible heritage التراث غير المادي كالأغاني والحرف والحكايات.\nقرائن السياق: التعريف بعد شرطة، والمثال بعد such as، والتضاد بعد unlike، والاستنتاج من الموقف.\nهذه الفروق الدقيقة أساس أسئلة Words in Context في SAT."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Restore, Renovate or Preserve? Conservation Vocabulary and Context Clues”. Let’s learn heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription together.","on_screen":"GV-L09-U3-LS3 | Restore, Renovate or Preserve? Conservation Vocabulary and Context Clues","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. craftsmanship: the skill with which something is made by hand. legacy: something important that people from the past leave for the future. vandalism: the crime of deliberately damaging public or private property.","on_screen":"craftsmanship | legacy | vandalism","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Words with related meanings: preserve = keep something as it is, stop it from changing; conserve = protect it carefully, especially from damage or decay; restore = return it to its original condition; renovate = repair and improve it, often with modern features; rebuild = build it again after it was destroyed. An authentic object is original; a replica is an exact copy. Heritage words: artifact (an old object made by people), inscription (words cut into stone), archaeologist / excavate (study the past by digging), landmark (a famous, recognizable place), craftsmanship (skill in making things by hand), legacy (what the past leaves us), intangible heritage (traditions, songs, skills – things you can't touch), vandalism (deliberate damage).","on_screen":"heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The museum works to preserve the manuscripts in a dark, cool room. The palace was restored using the original materials. The old house was renovated and turned into a modern café.","on_screen":"The museum works to preserve the manuscripts in a dark, cool room. / The palace was restored using the original materials. / The old house was renovated and turned into a modern café.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “They renovated the old palace exactly as it was in 1850.” That’s not right. We say: “They restored the old palace exactly as it was in 1850.” Original condition → restore.","on_screen":"✗ They renovated the old palace exactly as it was in 1850.   ✓ They restored the old palace exactly as it was in 1850.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: The old house now has glass walls and air conditioning. Was it restored or renovated? … Think! … Renovated – it was modernized. Great job! Now you can say: I can explain the difference between \"restore\" and \"renovate\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can explain the difference between \"restore\" and \"renovate\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","كلمات متقاربة: preserve (يحفظ كما هو)، conserve (يصون من التلف)، restore (يعيده إلى حالته الأصلية)، renovate (يجدّد ويحدّث)، rebuild (يعيد بناءه بعد تهدّمه).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: They renovated the old palace exactly as it was in 1850. — الصحيح: They restored the old palace exactly as it was in 1850.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أشرح الفرق بين restore وrenovate."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The palace was ___ using the original materials, so it looks exactly as it did in 1850.","options":["restored","renovated","rebuilt from glass","vandalized"],"answer":"restored","explanation":"Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."},{"q":"The old house was ___ and turned into a modern café with air conditioning.","options":["excavated","preserved","renovated","inscribed"],"answer":"renovated","explanation":"Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."},{"q":"Archaeologists ___ an ancient settlement near Tayma.","options":["vandalized","inscribed","excavated","renovated"],"answer":"excavated","explanation":"Heritage word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Folk songs and traditional dances are part of our ___ heritage.","options":["dilapidated","authentic","replica","intangible"],"answer":"intangible","explanation":"Heritage word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"\"The house was dilapidated—old, broken and falling apart.\" What type of clue explains \"dilapidated\"?","options":["a cause","a contrast","an example","a definition"],"answer":"a definition","explanation":"Use the context clue.","explanation_ar":"قرينة السياق."},{"q":"Because the original carved doors were too fragile to display outside, the museum placed exact ______ at the entrance and kept the real doors in a climate-controlled room.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["artifacts","replicas","landmarks","inscriptions"],"answer":"replicas","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"inscription","options":["the skill of making things by hand","a famous place that is easy to recognize","words cut into stone or metal","an old object made by people","deliberately damaging property","what people from the past leave for the future"],"answer":"words cut into stone or metal","explanation":"inscription → words cut into stone or metal. Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."},{"q":"landmark","options":["the skill of making things by hand","a famous place that is easy to recognize","words cut into stone or metal","an old object made by people","deliberately damaging property","what people from the past leave for the future"],"answer":"a famous place that is easy to recognize","explanation":"landmark → a famous place that is easy to recognize. Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."},{"q":"vandalism","options":["the skill of making things by hand","a famous place that is easy to recognize","words cut into stone or metal","an old object made by people","deliberately damaging property","what people from the past leave for the future"],"answer":"deliberately damaging property","explanation":"vandalism → deliberately damaging property. Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."},{"q":"craftsmanship","options":["the skill of making things by hand","a famous place that is easy to recognize","words cut into stone or metal","an old object made by people","deliberately damaging property","what people from the past leave for the future"],"answer":"the skill of making things by hand","explanation":"craftsmanship → the skill of making things by hand. Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."},{"q":"legacy","options":["the skill of making things by hand","a famous place that is easy to recognize","words cut into stone or metal","an old object made by people","deliberately damaging property","what people from the past leave for the future"],"answer":"what people from the past leave for the future","explanation":"legacy → what people from the past leave for the future. Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."},{"q":"artifact","options":["the skill of making things by hand","a famous place that is easy to recognize","words cut into stone or metal","an old object made by people","deliberately damaging property","what people from the past leave for the future"],"answer":"an old object made by people","explanation":"artifact → an old object made by people. Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Use conservation words.","items":[{"q":"Name a landmark in your city and describe it.","options":[],"answer":"The Shubra Palace is a landmark in Taif; it has beautiful wooden windows.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"preserve\".","options":[],"answer":"We must preserve our grandparents' stories by recording them.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"deteriorate\".","options":[],"answer":"Without repairs, the mud walls will deteriorate in the rain.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Name something that is part of Saudi Arabia's intangible heritage.","options":[],"answer":"The Ardah dance is part of Saudi Arabia's intangible heritage.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"authentic\".","options":[],"answer":"The museum shop sells authentic handmade baskets.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Heritage protection plan.","items":[{"q":"Choose a heritage site and write 3 sentences using restore, preserve and safeguard.","options":[],"answer":"The old souq should be restored to its original design. Its wooden doors must be preserved. New laws should safeguard it from demolition.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about how vandalism can be prevented.","options":[],"answer":"Cameras can be installed at the site. Visitors can be taught about the value of heritage.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with a context clue that explains a difficult word.","options":[],"answer":"The inscription—words carved into the rock thousands of years ago—was still readable.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"conservation","match":"the protection of buildings, nature or objects from damage","arabic":"الصون / الحفاظ"},{"word":"renovate","match":"to repair and improve an old building so it is in good condition","arabic":"يجدّد / يرمّم"},{"word":"authentic","match":"real and original, not a copy","arabic":"أصيل / أصلي"},{"word":"deteriorate","match":"to become worse in condition","arabic":"يتدهور"},{"word":"artifact","match":"an object made by people long ago that has historical interest","arabic":"قطعة أثرية"},{"word":"excavate","match":"to dig carefully to find old objects or buildings","arabic":"ينقّب"},{"word":"archaeologist","match":"a person who studies the past by digging up old objects and buildings","arabic":"عالِم آثار"},{"word":"landmark","match":"a famous building or place that is easy to recognize","arabic":"معلَم"},{"word":"craftsmanship","match":"the skill with which something is made by hand","arabic":"الإتقان الحِرفي"},{"word":"legacy","match":"something important that people from the past leave for the future","arabic":"إرث"},{"word":"vandalism","match":"the crime of deliberately damaging public or private property","arabic":"التخريب"},{"word":"intangible","match":"not physical; something you can't touch, such as traditions and songs","arabic":"غير مادي"},{"word":"dilapidated","match":"old and in very bad condition","arabic":"متهالك / متداعٍ"},{"word":"inscription","match":"words cut into stone or metal","arabic":"نقش"},{"word":"safeguard","match":"to protect something from harm or loss","arabic":"يصون / يحمي"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The museum keeps the manuscripts in a dark, cool room to ___ them.","options":["vandalize","preserve","excavate","renovate"],"answer":"preserve","explanation":"Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."},{"q":"After the earthquake destroyed the mosque, the villagers ___ it with the same stones.","options":["excavated","renovated with glass","rebuilt","preserved as ruins"],"answer":"rebuilt","explanation":"Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."},{"q":"The coins in the shop are ___, not authentic.","options":["artifacts","landmarks","legacies","replicas"],"answer":"replicas","explanation":"Heritage word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Someone sprayed paint on the ancient rock carvings. This is ___.","options":["excavation","craftsmanship","conservation","vandalism"],"answer":"vandalism","explanation":"Heritage word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Without regular repairs, old mud buildings quickly ___.","options":["deteriorate","renovate","excavate","safeguard"],"answer":"deteriorate","explanation":"Heritage word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The ___ on the stone was written in an ancient Arabian script.","options":["legacy","inscription","landmark","replica"],"answer":"inscription","explanation":"Heritage word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The beautiful carving shows the ___ of the old builders.","options":["deterioration","craftsmanship","vandalism","excavation"],"answer":"craftsmanship","explanation":"Heritage word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"\"Unlike the authentic coins, the copies were made of plastic.\" What clue helps us understand \"authentic\"?","options":["the contrast word \"Unlike\"","the word \"plastic\" alone","the period","the word \"coins\""],"answer":"the contrast word \"Unlike\"","explanation":"Use the context clue.","explanation_ar":"قرينة السياق."},{"q":"The once-grand house had become so ______ that its roof leaked, its walls were cracked and its staircase could no longer be used.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["authentic","intangible","renovated","dilapidated"],"answer":"dilapidated","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."},{"q":"For the elderly craftsman, teaching young people to carve wooden doors was a way to ______ a skill that might otherwise disappear within a generation.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["deteriorate","vandalize","safeguard","excavate"],"answer":"safeguard","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"Three versions of the same old house: \"dilapidated\" (broken windows, cracked walls), \"restored\" (looking exactly as it did 200 years ago) and \"renovated\" (old walls with modern glass and air conditioning); an archaeologist brushing sand from an inscription in the background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Three versions of the same old house: \"dilapidated\" (broken windows, cracked walls), \"restored\" (looking exactly as it did 200 years ago) and \"renovated\" (old walls with modern glass and air conditioning); an archaeologist brushing sand from an inscription in the background"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows craftsmanship (the skill with which something is made by hand); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing craftsmanship: the skill with which something is made by hand"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows legacy (something important that people from the past leave for the future); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing legacy: something important that people from the past leave for the future"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows vandalism (the crime of deliberately damaging public or private property); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing vandalism: the crime of deliberately damaging public or private property"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows intangible (not physical; something you can't touch, such as traditions and songs); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing intangible: not physical; something you can't touch, such as traditions and songs"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows dilapidated (old and in very bad condition); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing dilapidated: old and in very bad condition"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows inscription (words cut into stone or metal); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing inscription: words cut into stone or metal"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-W07","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows safeguard (to protect something from harm or loss); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing safeguard: to protect something from harm or loss"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W01","script":"craftsmanship. craftsmanship. The doors show amazing craftsmanship.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W02","script":"legacy. legacy. The old mosques are part of our grandparents' legacy.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W03","script":"vandalism. vandalism. Vandalism has damaged several ancient rock carvings.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W04","script":"intangible. intangible. Arabic calligraphy is part of the world's intangible cultural heritage.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W05","script":"dilapidated. dilapidated. The dilapidated house was finally restored.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W06","script":"inscription. inscription. Ancient inscriptions were found on the rocks near Tayma.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-W07","script":"safeguard. safeguard. New laws safeguard historic buildings.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Restore, Renovate or Preserve? Conservation Vocabulary and Context Clues”. Let’s learn heritage conservation vocabulary; nuances between restore / renovate / preserve / conserve / rebuild; authentic vs replica; context clues (definition, example, contrast, inference) for words such as dilapidated, intangible and inscription together. Meet some new words. craftsmanship: the skill with which something is made by hand. legacy: something important that people from the past leave for the future. vandalism: the crime of deliberately damaging public or private property. Words with related meanings: preserve = keep something as it is, stop it from changing; conserve = protect it carefully, especially from damage or decay; restore = return it to its original condition; renovate = repair and improve it, often with modern features; rebuild = build it again after it was destroyed. An authentic object is original; a replica is an exact copy. Heritage words: artifact (an old object made by people), inscription (words cut into stone), archaeologist / excavate (study the past by digging), landmark (a famous, recognizable place), craftsmanship (skill in making things by hand), legacy (what the past leaves us), intangible heritage (traditions, songs, skills – things you can't touch), vandalism (deliberate damage). Here are some examples. The museum works to preserve the manuscripts in a dark, cool room. The palace was restored using the original materials. The old house was renovated and turned into a modern café. Be careful! Some learners say: “They renovated the old palace exactly as it was in 1850.” That’s not right. We say: “They restored the old palace exactly as it was in 1850.” Original condition → restore. Quick check: The old house now has glass walls and air conditioning. Was it restored or renovated? … Think! … Renovated – it was modernized. Great job! Now you can say: I can explain the difference between \"restore\" and \"renovate\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS4","title":"Not Only to Protect but Also to Teach: Parallel Structure","objectives":["Students will be able to write lists, pairs and comparisons in parallel form.","Students will be able to use correlative conjunctions with matching grammatical structures.","I can write \"The project aims to protect, restore and promote the old souq.\"","I can write \"The museum is not only educational but also entertaining.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة القوائم والأزواج والمقارنات بتراكيب متوازية.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام أدوات الربط المزدوجة مع تراكيب نحوية متطابقة.","أستطيع أن أكتب The project aims to protect, restore and promote the old souq.","أستطيع أن أكتب The museum is not only educational but also entertaining."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"conservation","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌkɑnsɚˈveɪʃən/","definition":"the protection of buildings, nature or objects from damage","arabic":"الصون / الحفاظ","example":"The conservation of old manuscripts requires special skills.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"renovate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈrɛnəˌveɪt/","definition":"to repair and improve an old building so it is in good condition","arabic":"يجدّد / يرمّم","example":"They renovated the old house and added a modern kitchen.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"authentic","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/əˈθɛntɪk/","definition":"real and original, not a copy","arabic":"أصيل / أصلي","example":"The museum displays authentic tools from the Nabataean period.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"deteriorate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/dɪˈtɪriɚˌeɪt/","definition":"to become worse in condition","arabic":"يتدهور","example":"Without care, the old walls will deteriorate quickly.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"artifact","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɑrtəˌfækt/","definition":"an object made by people long ago that has historical interest","arabic":"قطعة أثرية","example":"Archaeologists found pottery and other artifacts at the site.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"excavate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈɛkskəˌveɪt/","definition":"to dig carefully to find old objects or buildings","arabic":"ينقّب","example":"The team excavated an ancient settlement near Al-Ula.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Parallel structure means using the same grammatical form for items that do the same job. In a list: The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and planted trees. (all past simple verbs) NOT (not: cleaned the site, repairing the walls and they planted trees).\nWith correlative conjunctions, the structures after each part must match: both the old mosque and the souq (noun + noun); either to restore it or to rebuild it (infinitive + infinitive); not only protects buildings but also teaches young people (verb + verb); neither by car nor by bus (prepositional phrase + prepositional phrase).\nIn comparisons, compare the same kinds of things and forms: Restoring a house is harder than building a new one. (-ing vs -ing) To preserve is better than to rebuild. SAT questions often test whether the last item in a list or the second part of a correlative pair matches the first.\nlists: same form for every item (verb, -ing, to + verb, noun, clause)\nboth… and / either… or / neither… nor / not only… but also → matching structures\ncomparisons: compare like with like (-ing with -ing, to with to)\ncheck the last item and the second half of a pair","examples":["The project aims to protect, to restore and to promote the old souq.","Visitors can walk through the lanes, visit the museum and buy local crafts.","The house was old, dark and dilapidated.","The craftsmen work both carefully and quickly.","The site is not only historically important but also beautiful.","You can either take the guided tour or explore on your own.","Restoring old houses is more expensive than demolishing them.","The archaeologists found that the city was large and that it traded with Yemen."],"common_errors":["✗ The volunteers cleaned the site, repairing the walls and planted trees. → ✓ The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and planted trees. (All past simple.)","✗ The museum is not only educational but also it entertains. → ✓ The museum is not only educational but also entertaining. (adjective + adjective.)","✗ Either we restore the fort or rebuilding it. → ✓ Either we restore the fort or we rebuild it. (clause + clause.)","✗ Preserving a manuscript is harder than to copy it. → ✓ Preserving a manuscript is harder than copying it. (-ing + -ing.)"],"arabic":"التوازي يعني استخدام الصيغة النحوية نفسها للعناصر التي تؤدي الوظيفة نفسها: cleaned, repaired and planted.\nمع أدوات الربط المزدوجة (both… and / either… or / neither… nor / not only… but also) يجب أن يتطابق التركيب بعد كل جزء.\nفي المقارنات نقارن الشيء بمثله: Restoring… than demolishing…\nأسئلة SAT تختبر غالبًا العنصر الأخير في القائمة أو الجزء الثاني من الزوج."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Not Only to Protect but Also to Teach: Parallel Structure”. Let’s learn parallel structure in lists, pairs and comparisons; correlative conjunctions (both… and, either… or, neither… nor, not only… but also); parallel verb forms (-ing / to / base / clauses); parallelism in SAT items together.","on_screen":"GV-L09-U3-LS4 | Not Only to Protect but Also to Teach: Parallel Structure","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Parallel structure means using the same grammatical form for items that do the same job. In a list: The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and planted trees. (all past simple verbs) NOT (not: cleaned the site, repairing the walls and they planted trees).","on_screen":"parallel structure in lists, pairs and comparisons; correlative conjunctions (both… and, either… or, neither… nor, not only… but also); parallel verb forms (-ing / to / base / clauses); parallelism in SAT items","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Parallel structure means using the same grammatical form for items that do the same job. In a list: The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and planted trees. (all past simple verbs) NOT (not: cleaned the site, repairing the walls and they planted trees). With correlative conjunctions, the structures after each part must match: both the old mosque and the souq (noun + noun); either to restore it or to rebuild it (infinitive + infinitive); not only protects buildings but also teaches young people (verb + verb); neither by car nor by bus (prepositional phrase + prepositional phrase).","on_screen":"lists: same form for every item (verb, -ing, to + verb, noun, clause) • both… and / either… or / neither… nor / not only… but also → matching structures • comparisons: compare like with like (-ing with -ing, to with to)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The project aims to protect, to restore and to promote the old souq. Visitors can walk through the lanes, visit the museum and buy local crafts. The house was old, dark and dilapidated.","on_screen":"The project aims to protect, to restore and to promote the old souq. / Visitors can walk through the lanes, visit the museum and buy local crafts. / The house was old, dark and dilapidated.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The volunteers cleaned the site, repairing the walls and planted trees.” That’s not right. We say: “The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and planted trees.” All past simple.","on_screen":"✗ The volunteers cleaned the site, repairing the walls and planted trees.   ✓ The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and planted trees.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: \"The house was old, dark and falling.\" Is this parallel? … Think! … Not quite – better: *old, dark and dilapidated* (three adjectives). Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"The project aims to protect, restore and promote the old souq.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"The project aims to protect, restore and promote the old souq.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: parallel structure in lists, pairs and comparisons; correlative conjunctions (both… and, either… or, neither… nor, not only… but also); parallel verb forms (-ing / to / base / clauses); parallelism in SAT items.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","التوازي يعني استخدام الصيغة النحوية نفسها للعناصر التي تؤدي الوظيفة نفسها: cleaned, repaired and planted.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The volunteers cleaned the site, repairing the walls and planted trees. — الصحيح: The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and planted trees.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب The project aims to protect, restore and promote the old souq."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Restoring the Old Fort (editing passage)","body":"The restoration team had three goals: to repair the walls, rebuilding the towers and to open a small museum. The workers were careful, patient and they had skill. They used not only traditional mud bricks but also used palm wood. Repairing the old gate was harder than to build a new one. Today, the fort is both a landmark and educates visitors.","word_count":62,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and ___ trees.","options":["to plant","planted","planting","they planted"],"answer":"planted","explanation":"Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"The museum is not only educational but also ___.","options":["entertaining","it entertains","to entertain","entertainment is"],"answer":"entertaining","explanation":"Correlative conjunctions with matching structures.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط المزدوجة."},{"q":"Restoring an old house is often more expensive than ___ a new one.","options":["build","built","building","to build"],"answer":"building","explanation":"Parallel comparison.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في المقارنة."},{"q":"You can either take the guided tour or ___ on your own.","options":["exploring","explored","to explore","explore"],"answer":"explore","explanation":"Correlative conjunctions with matching structures.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط المزدوجة."},{"q":"","options":["The project aims to protect, to restore and promoting the old souq.","The project aims to protect, restoring and promotion of the old souq.","The project aims protecting, to restore and to promote the old souq.","The project aims to protect, to restore and to promote the old souq."],"answer":"The project aims to protect, to restore and to promote the old souq.","explanation":"Matching verb forms (-ing / to / base / clause).","explanation_ar":"تطابق صيغ الأفعال."},{"q":"The restoration team spent months studying old photographs, interviewing elderly residents and ______ the original building techniques.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["tested","to test","testing","they tested"],"answer":"testing","explanation":"Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في القائمة."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS4-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct parallel form. Word bank: quickly, copying, dilapidated","items":[{"q":"The old house was dark, damp and ______ (dilapidate).","options":[],"answer":"dilapidated","explanation":"Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"The craftsmen work both carefully and ______ (quick).","options":[],"answer":"quickly","explanation":"Correlative conjunctions with matching structures.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط المزدوجة."},{"q":"Preserving a manuscript is harder than ______ (copy) it.","options":[],"answer":"copying","explanation":"Parallel comparison.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في المقارنة."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"Visitors can walk through the lanes, visit the museum and buying local crafts.","options":[],"answer":"Visitors can walk through the lanes, visit the museum and buy local crafts.","explanation":"buying → buy. Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: buying → buy. التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"The site is not only important but also it is beautiful.","options":[],"answer":"The site is not only important but also beautiful.","explanation":"but also it is beautiful → but also beautiful. Correlative conjunctions with matching structures.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: but also it is beautiful → but also beautiful. أدوات الربط المزدوجة."},{"q":"Neither the fort or the mosque was damaged in the storm.","options":[],"answer":"Neither the fort nor the mosque was damaged in the storm.","explanation":"or → nor. Correlative conjunctions with matching structures.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: or → nor. أدوات الربط المزدوجة."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the restoration report.","items":[{"q":"The restoration team had three goals: to repair the walls, rebuilding the towers and to open a small museum.","options":[],"answer":"The restoration team had three goals: to repair the walls, to rebuild the towers and to open a small museum.","explanation":"rebuilding → to rebuild. Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: rebuilding → to rebuild. التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"The workers were careful, patient and they had skill.","options":[],"answer":"The workers were careful, patient and skillful.","explanation":"they had skill → skillful. Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: they had skill → skillful. التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"They used not only traditional mud bricks but also used palm wood.","options":[],"answer":"They used not only traditional mud bricks but also palm wood.","explanation":"but also used → but also. Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: but also used → but also. التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"Repairing the old gate was harder than to build a new one.","options":[],"answer":"Repairing the old gate was harder than building a new one.","explanation":"to build → building. Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: to build → building. التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"Today, the fort is both a landmark and educates visitors.","options":[],"answer":"Today, the fort is both a landmark and a classroom for visitors.","explanation":"and educates visitors → and a classroom for visitors. Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: and educates visitors → and a classroom for visitors. التوازي في القائمة."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write parallel sentences.","items":[{"q":"Write a list of three things volunteers can do to protect a heritage site (same form).","options":[],"answer":"Volunteers can clean the site, guide visitors and report damage.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses parallel structure in lists, pairs and comparisons; correlative conjunctions (both… and, either… or, neither… nor, not only… but also); parallel verb forms (-ing / to / base / clauses); parallelism in SAT items correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"not only… but also\" about a museum.","options":[],"answer":"The museum not only displays artifacts but also teaches traditional crafts.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses parallel structure in lists, pairs and comparisons; correlative conjunctions (both… and, either… or, neither… nor, not only… but also); parallel verb forms (-ing / to / base / clauses); parallelism in SAT items correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a comparison with two -ing forms.","options":[],"answer":"Visiting a real heritage site is more exciting than reading about it.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses parallel structure in lists, pairs and comparisons; correlative conjunctions (both… and, either… or, neither… nor, not only… but also); parallel verb forms (-ing / to / base / clauses); parallelism in SAT items correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Builder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The teacher reads a word and a short clue.","Teams build the word with letter tiles in 30 seconds.","The team holds up the word; correct spelling = 1 point, with correct capital letter or punctuation where needed = 1 bonus point.","Continue until all words are used."],"data":[{"word":"conservation","clue":"the protection of buildings, nature or objects from damage"},{"word":"archaeologist","clue":"a person who studies the past by digging up old objects and buildings"},{"word":"artifact","clue":"an object made by people long ago that has historical interest"},{"word":"authentic","clue":"real and original, not a copy"},{"word":"craftsmanship","clue":"the skill with which something is made by hand"},{"word":"legacy","clue":"something important that people from the past leave for the future"},{"word":"renovate","clue":"to repair and improve an old building so it is in good condition"},{"word":"deteriorate","clue":"to become worse in condition"},{"word":"excavate","clue":"to dig carefully to find old objects or buildings"},{"word":"landmark","clue":"a famous building or place that is easy to recognize"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The archaeologists measured, photographed and ___ every object.","options":["they recorded","recorded","to record","recording"],"answer":"recorded","explanation":"Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"The souq is both a shopping center and ___.","options":["where people meet","a meeting place","to meet","meeting people in"],"answer":"a meeting place","explanation":"Correlative conjunctions with matching structures.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط المزدوجة."},{"q":"Learning a traditional craft takes longer than ___ a factory-made product.","options":["bought","buy","to buy","buying"],"answer":"buying","explanation":"Parallel comparison.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في المقارنة."},{"q":"","options":["Neither the guide or the visitors knew the history of the inscription.","Neither the guide nor did the visitors know the history of the inscription.","Not the guide nor the visitors knew the history of the inscription.","Neither the guide nor the visitors knew the history of the inscription."],"answer":"Neither the guide nor the visitors knew the history of the inscription.","explanation":"Correlative conjunctions with matching structures.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط المزدوجة."},{"q":"","options":["The festival celebrates poetry, music and traditional dance.","The festival celebrates poetry, playing music and dance.","The festival celebrates poetry, music and dancing traditionally.","The festival celebrates poetry, music and to dance."],"answer":"The festival celebrates poetry, music and traditional dance.","explanation":"Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"Which sentence is NOT parallel?","options":["The old houses were tall and narrow, and they were made of coral stone.","The old houses were tall, narrow and they were made of coral stone.","The old houses were tall, narrow and beautiful.","The old houses were tall, narrow and coral-stone."],"answer":"The old houses were tall, narrow and they were made of coral stone.","explanation":"Choose the best correction.","explanation_ar":"أفضل تصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["Either we protect the site now, or to lose it forever.","Either we protect the site now, or losing it forever.","Either protecting the site now, or we lose it forever.","Either we protect the site now, or we lose it forever."],"answer":"Either we protect the site now, or we lose it forever.","explanation":"Matching verb forms (-ing / to / base / clause).","explanation_ar":"تطابق صيغ الأفعال."},{"q":"The new heritage law requires owners of historic buildings to maintain the original facades, use traditional materials and ______ permission before making any changes.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["obtaining","to obtaining","obtain","they obtain"],"answer":"obtain","explanation":"Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"The Saudi Heritage Commission works not only to protect ancient sites ______ young Saudis about their history.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["but also to educate","and also education","but also it educates","but also educating"],"answer":"but also to educate","explanation":"Correlative conjunctions with matching structures.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط المزدوجة."},{"q":"According to the architects, restoring the old palace was more challenging than ______ the modern museum next to it.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["design","they designed","designing","to design"],"answer":"designing","explanation":"Parallel comparison.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في المقارنة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Protecting Our Heritage” that shows parallel structure in lists, pairs and comparisons; correlative conjunctions (both… and, either… or, neither… nor, not only… but also); parallel verb forms (-ing / to / base / clauses); parallelism in SAT items in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Protecting Our Heritage” that shows parallel structure in lists, pairs and comparisons; correlative conjunctions (both… and, either… or, neither… nor, not only… but also); parallel verb forms (-ing / to / base / clauses); parallelism in SAT items in action"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Builder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Builder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Not Only to Protect but Also to Teach: Parallel Structure”. Let’s learn parallel structure in lists, pairs and comparisons; correlative conjunctions (both… and, either… or, neither… nor, not only… but also); parallel verb forms (-ing / to / base / clauses); parallelism in SAT items together. Parallel structure means using the same grammatical form for items that do the same job. In a list: The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and planted trees. (all past simple verbs) NOT (not: cleaned the site, repairing the walls and they planted trees). Parallel structure means using the same grammatical form for items that do the same job. In a list: The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and planted trees. (all past simple verbs) NOT (not: cleaned the site, repairing the walls and they planted trees). With correlative conjunctions, the structures after each part must match: both the old mosque and the souq (noun + noun); either to restore it or to rebuild it (infinitive + infinitive); not only protects buildings but also teaches young people (verb + verb); neither by car nor by bus (prepositional phrase + prepositional phrase). Here are some examples. The project aims to protect, to restore and to promote the old souq. Visitors can walk through the lanes, visit the museum and buy local crafts. The house was old, dark and dilapidated. Be careful! Some learners say: “The volunteers cleaned the site, repairing the walls and planted trees.” That’s not right. We say: “The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and planted trees.” All past simple. Quick check: \"The house was old, dark and falling.\" Is this parallel? … Think! … Not quite – better: *old, dark and dilapidated* (three adjectives). Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"The project aims to protect, restore and promote the old souq.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS5","title":"A Proposal to Save the Old Souq: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to debate how a heritage site should be protected.","Students will be able to write a formal proposal with advanced passives, precise vocabulary and parallel structure, and answer SAT-style transition and synthesis items.","I can argue for the best way to protect a heritage site.","I can write a formal heritage proposal."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من مناقشة كيفية حماية موقع تراثي.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة مقترح رسمي بصيغ المجهول المتقدمة والمفردات الدقيقة والتوازي، والإجابة عن أسئلة الروابط والتركيب بنمط SAT.","أستطيع أن أدافع عن أفضل طريقة لحماية موقع تراثي.","أستطيع أن أكتب مقترحًا رسميًّا لحماية التراث."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"conservation","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌkɑnsɚˈveɪʃən/","definition":"the protection of buildings, nature or objects from damage","arabic":"الصون / الحفاظ","example":"The conservation of old manuscripts requires special skills.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"renovate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈrɛnəˌveɪt/","definition":"to repair and improve an old building so it is in good condition","arabic":"يجدّد / يرمّم","example":"They renovated the old house and added a modern kitchen.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"authentic","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/əˈθɛntɪk/","definition":"real and original, not a copy","arabic":"أصيل / أصلي","example":"The museum displays authentic tools from the Nabataean period.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"deteriorate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/dɪˈtɪriɚˌeɪt/","definition":"to become worse in condition","arabic":"يتدهور","example":"Without care, the old walls will deteriorate quickly.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"artifact","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɑrtəˌfækt/","definition":"an object made by people long ago that has historical interest","arabic":"قطعة أثرية","example":"Archaeologists found pottery and other artifacts at the site.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"excavate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈɛkskəˌveɪt/","definition":"to dig carefully to find old objects or buildings","arabic":"ينقّب","example":"The team excavated an ancient settlement near Al-Ula.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"archaeologist","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɑrkiˈɑlədʒɪst/","definition":"a person who studies the past by digging up old objects and buildings","arabic":"عالِم آثار","example":"The archaeologist cleaned the coin with a soft brush.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"landmark","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlændˌmɑrk/","definition":"a famous building or place that is easy to recognize","arabic":"معلَم","example":"The Kingdom Centre is a famous Riyadh landmark.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"craftsmanship","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkræftsmənˌʃɪp/","definition":"the skill with which something is made by hand","arabic":"الإتقان الحِرفي","example":"The doors show amazing craftsmanship.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"legacy","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɛɡəsi/","definition":"something important that people from the past leave for the future","arabic":"إرث","example":"The old mosques are part of our grandparents' legacy.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"vandalism","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvændəlɪzəm/","definition":"the crime of deliberately damaging public or private property","arabic":"التخريب","example":"Vandalism has damaged several ancient rock carvings.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"intangible","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈtændʒəbəl/","definition":"not physical; something you can't touch, such as traditions and songs","arabic":"غير مادي","example":"Arabic calligraphy is part of the world's intangible cultural heritage.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"dilapidated","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/dəˈlæpəˌdeɪtɪd/","definition":"old and in very bad condition","arabic":"متهالك / متداعٍ","example":"The dilapidated house was finally restored.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"inscription","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈskrɪpʃən/","definition":"words cut into stone or metal","arabic":"نقش","example":"Ancient inscriptions were found on the rocks near Tayma.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"safeguard","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈseɪfˌɡɑrd/","definition":"to protect something from harm or loss","arabic":"يصون / يحمي","example":"New laws safeguard historic buildings.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 3: advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary and parallel structure.\nA formal proposal describes the problem, gives evidence, makes a clear recommendation, explains the steps and the benefits, and warns about the consequences of doing nothing. Passive forms keep the focus on the site; parallel structure makes lists of steps clear and powerful.\n✔ is being / has been / should be / should have been + past participle\n✔ is thought to have been built • it was once believed that\n✔ preserve, restore, renovate, authentic, legacy, safeguard\n✔ parallel lists • not only… but also","examples":["The souq is thought to have been built in the 1820s.","Its roofs have been damaged by heavy rain.","The project should have been started years ago.","The walls are being checked by engineers this month.","The souq must be protected from being demolished.","The plan aims to restore the buildings, to support local shops and to attract visitors.","The souq is not only a market but also a living museum.","Moreover, restoring the souq will create jobs for young craftsmen."],"common_errors":["✗ The souq is thought to have built in the 1820s. → ✓ The souq is thought to have been built in the 1820s. (Passive → to have been + past participle.)","✗ The roofs should have repaired years ago. → ✓ The roofs should have been repaired years ago. (Modal past passive.)","✗ The plan aims to restore the buildings, supporting shops and to attract visitors. → ✓ … to restore the buildings, to support shops and to attract visitors. (Parallel infinitives.)"],"arabic":"نراجع صيغ المجهول المتقدمة وتراكيب النقل المبنية للمجهول ومفردات الحفاظ على التراث والتوازي.\nالمقترح الرسمي يصف المشكلة ويقدّم الأدلة ويوصي بحل واضح ويشرح الخطوات والفوائد وعواقب عدم التحرك.\nالمجهول يُبقي التركيز على الموقع، والتوازي يجعل قوائم الخطوات واضحة وقوية."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Proposal to Save the Old Souq: Language in Use”. Let’s learn advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L09-U3-LS5 | A Proposal to Save the Old Souq: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Heritage council debate: groups represent the town council, local shop owners, archaeologists and young people. Each group argues whether the old souq should be restored, renovated or demolished, using two advanced passives, one passive reporting structure and one parallel sentence. The class votes.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 3: advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary and parallel structure. A formal proposal describes the problem, gives evidence, makes a clear recommendation, explains the steps and the benefits, and warns about the consequences of doing nothing. Passive forms keep the focus on the site; parallel structure makes lists of steps clear and powerful.","on_screen":"✔ is being / has been / should be / should have been + past participle • ✔ is thought to have been built • it was once believed that • ✔ preserve, restore, renovate, authentic, legacy, safeguard","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The souq is thought to have been built in the 1820s. Its roofs have been damaged by heavy rain. The project should have been started years ago.","on_screen":"The souq is thought to have been built in the 1820s. / Its roofs have been damaged by heavy rain. / The project should have been started years ago.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The souq is thought to have built in the 1820s.” That’s not right. We say: “The souq is thought to have been built in the 1820s.” Passive → to have been + past participle.","on_screen":"✗ The souq is thought to have built in the 1820s.   ✓ The souq is thought to have been built in the 1820s.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “The roofs should have repaired years ago.”? … Think! … It should be “The roofs should have been repaired years ago.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can argue for the best way to protect a heritage site.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can argue for the best way to protect a heritage site.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع صيغ المجهول المتقدمة وتراكيب النقل المبنية للمجهول ومفردات الحفاظ على التراث والتوازي.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The souq is thought to have built in the 1820s. — الصحيح: The souq is thought to have been built in the 1820s.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أدافع عن أفضل طريقة لحماية موقع تراثي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"A Proposal to Save the Old Souq – Omar's Group","body":"The old souq in our town, which is thought to have been built over two hundred years ago, is in urgent need of attention.\nMany of its wooden doors have been damaged by sun and rain, and several roofs are believed to be unsafe.\nWe propose that the souq be restored, not demolished.\nFirst, the buildings should be surveyed by experts; next, damaged materials should be repaired or replaced with authentic ones; finally, local craftsmen should be invited to train young people.\nOnce it has been restored, the souq could become a center not only for tourism but also for culture and traditional crafts.\nHowever, if it is not protected now, an important part of our legacy will be lost forever.","word_count":121,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the proposal. True or False?","items":[{"q":"The souq is thought to be over two hundred years old.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Proposal to Save the Old Souq – Omar's Group”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The wooden doors are in perfect condition.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Proposal to Save the Old Souq – Omar's Group”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The group proposes that the souq be demolished.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Proposal to Save the Old Souq – Omar's Group”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The buildings should be surveyed by experts first.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Proposal to Save the Old Souq – Omar's Group”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Local craftsmen should be invited to train young people.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Proposal to Save the Old Souq – Omar's Group”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The group thinks the souq could only be used for shopping.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Proposal to Save the Old Souq – Omar's Group”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"The souq is thought ___ over two hundred years ago.","options":["to have been built","to build","to have built","being built"],"answer":"to have been built","explanation":"Advanced passive or passive reporting structure.","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول المتقدم."},{"q":"Many of its wooden doors ___ by sun and rain.","options":["have damaged","are damaging","have been damaged","had damaging"],"answer":"have been damaged","explanation":"Advanced passive or passive reporting structure.","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول المتقدم."},{"q":"The group proposes that the souq be ___, not demolished.","options":["renovated with glass","restored","vandalized","excavated"],"answer":"restored","explanation":"Conservation vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"مفردات الحفاظ على التراث."},{"q":"","options":["The buildings should survey, repaired and protected.","The buildings should be surveyed, repairing and protected.","The buildings should be surveyed, repaired and to protect.","The buildings should be surveyed, repaired and protected."],"answer":"The buildings should be surveyed, repaired and protected.","explanation":"Parallel structure.","explanation_ar":"التوازي."},{"q":"The souq could become a center not only for tourism but also ___.","options":["culture and crafts are","it is for culture","for culture and crafts","to culture and crafts"],"answer":"for culture and crafts","explanation":"Parallel structure.","explanation_ar":"التوازي."},{"q":"Restoring the souq would cost more than demolishing it. ______ a restored souq would attract visitors and create jobs for many years.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["However,","Therefore,","For example,","Similarly,"],"answer":"However,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Heritage council debate: write your notes.","items":[{"q":"Your group and position: ___","options":[],"answer":"Shop owners – we want the souq renovated with air conditioning.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An advanced passive sentence for your argument: ___","options":[],"answer":"Our shops are being damaged by heat every summer.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A passive reporting structure: ___","options":[],"answer":"The souq is known to have been the main market for over a century.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A parallel sentence for your argument: ___","options":[],"answer":"A renovated souq would be cooler, safer and more attractive to customers.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A response to another group: ___","options":[],"answer":"We agree that the old doors should be preserved, but the roofs must be renovated.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your proposal.","items":[{"q":"Plan: site, history, problem, recommendation, three steps, benefits, warning.","options":[],"answer":"old fort near our village; thought to have been built in 1800s; walls deteriorating, vandalism; restore it; survey, repair with mud bricks, open a museum; tourism, education, jobs; if not protected, it will be lost","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your proposal in 8–9 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"The old fort near our village is believed to have been built in the early 1800s. Unfortunately, its walls have been badly damaged by rain, and several towers are collapsing. The fort has also been affected by vandalism. We propose that the fort be restored using traditional mud bricks. First, the site should be surveyed; then, damaged walls should be repaired; finally, a small museum should be opened inside. The fort would not only attract tourists but also teach young people about their history. Moreover, restoration work would create jobs for local craftsmen. If nothing is done, this important landmark will be lost forever.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: passive forms correct? parallel lists and correlative pairs? conservation words used precisely? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"The fort would not only attract tourists but also it teaches\" to \"would not only attract tourists but also teach\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Quiz Show Challenge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams take turns choosing a category and a cue word.","Grammar: make a sentence with advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review). Words: give the meaning. Spelling: spell it. Write It!: write a sentence with correct punctuation.","Correct answers score 10 points; teams may steal a question another team misses.","The highest score after 8 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"conservation","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"renovate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"authentic","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"deteriorate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"artifact","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"excavate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"archaeologist","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"landmark","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"craftsmanship","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"legacy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"vandalism","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"intangible","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"dilapidated","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"inscription","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"safeguard","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The old manuscripts ___ by experts at the moment.","options":["are restoring","are being restored","restored","have restoring"],"answer":"are being restored","explanation":"Advanced passive or passive reporting structure.","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول المتقدم."},{"q":"It ___ that the old well was dug by the village's founder.","options":["is saying","said it","says","is said"],"answer":"is said","explanation":"Advanced passive or passive reporting structure.","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول المتقدم."},{"q":"Keeping the manuscripts in a cool, dark room helps to ___ them.","options":["renovate","demolish","preserve","excavate"],"answer":"preserve","explanation":"Conservation vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"مفردات الحفاظ على التراث."},{"q":"The carved doors show the amazing ___ of the old builders.","options":["vandalism","craftsmanship","replica","excavation"],"answer":"craftsmanship","explanation":"Conservation vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"مفردات الحفاظ على التراث."},{"q":"","options":["The volunteers cleaning, painted and decorated the old school.","The volunteers cleaned, painted and decoration of the old school.","The volunteers cleaned, painting and decorated the old school.","The volunteers cleaned, painted and decorated the old school."],"answer":"The volunteers cleaned, painted and decorated the old school.","explanation":"Parallel structure.","explanation_ar":"التوازي."},{"q":"Heritage sites attract millions of visitors every year. ______ they can provide jobs for local guides, craftsmen and shop owners.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["As a result,","However,","Nevertheless,","In contrast,"],"answer":"As a result,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"Many people think that heritage only means old buildings. ______ songs, recipes and traditional skills are also part of our heritage.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Therefore,","For this reason,","In fact,","Similarly,"],"answer":"In fact,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Al-Ula contains thousands of years of history.\n• Hegra, in Al-Ula, was Saudi Arabia's first UNESCO World Heritage Site.\n• Hegra has more than 100 monumental tombs.\n• The tombs were carved by the Nabataeans.\n\nThe student wants to emphasize Hegra's international importance. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Hegra, with more than 100 monumental Nabataean tombs, was Saudi Arabia's first site to be added to the UNESCO World Heritage List.","The Nabataeans carved tombs.","Hegra is in Al-Ula.","Al-Ula contains thousands of years of history."],"answer":"Hegra, with more than 100 monumental Nabataean tombs, was Saudi Arabia's first site to be added to the UNESCO World Heritage List.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Many traditional crafts are disappearing.\n• Young people rarely learn them.\n• Some heritage centers offer free workshops.\n• In these workshops, elderly craftsmen teach weaving and pottery.\n\nThe student wants to present a solution to the loss of traditional crafts. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Free workshops in which elderly craftsmen teach weaving and pottery can help young people learn crafts that might otherwise disappear.","Many traditional crafts are disappearing.","Young people rarely learn traditional crafts.","Some heritage centers exist in Saudi Arabia."],"answer":"Free workshops in which elderly craftsmen teach weaving and pottery can help young people learn crafts that might otherwise disappear.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a heritage proposal:","options":["The old souq should be restored, protected and opening to visitors.","The old souq should be restored, protected and opened to visitors, not only for tourism but also for education.","The old souq should be restoring, protected and open visitors, not only tourism but education.","The old souq should restore, protecting and opened to visitors, not only for tourism but also it educates."],"answer":"The old souq should be restored, protected and opened to visitors, not only for tourism but also for education.","explanation":"Parallel structure.","explanation_ar":"التوازي."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A town council meeting: students presenting a proposal with photos of an old souq (cracked wooden doors, broken roofs) next to a drawing of the restored souq full of visitors and craftsmen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A town council meeting: students presenting a proposal with photos of an old souq (cracked wooden doors, broken roofs) next to a drawing of the restored souq full of visitors and craftsmen"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Protecting Our Heritage”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Protecting Our Heritage”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L09-U3-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Quiz Show Challenge”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Quiz Show Challenge"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS5-T1","script":"The old souq in our town, which is thought to have been built over two hundred years ago, is in urgent need of attention. Many of its wooden doors have been damaged by sun and rain, and several roofs are believed to be unsafe. We propose that the souq be restored, not demolished. First, the buildings should be surveyed by experts; next, damaged materials should be repaired or replaced with authentic ones; finally, local craftsmen should be invited to train young people. Once it has been restored, the souq could become a center not only for tourism but also for culture and traditional crafts. However, if it is not protected now, an important part of our legacy will be lost forever.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L09-U3-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Proposal to Save the Old Souq: Language in Use”. Let’s learn advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary, parallel structure; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Heritage council debate: groups represent the town council, local shop owners, archaeologists and young people. Each group argues whether the old souq should be restored, renovated or demolished, using two advanced passives, one passive reporting structure and one parallel sentence. The class votes. Today you use all of Unit 3: advanced passive forms, passive reporting structures, conservation vocabulary and parallel structure. A formal proposal describes the problem, gives evidence, makes a clear recommendation, explains the steps and the benefits, and warns about the consequences of doing nothing. Passive forms keep the focus on the site; parallel structure makes lists of steps clear and powerful. Here are some examples. The souq is thought to have been built in the 1820s. Its roofs have been damaged by heavy rain. The project should have been started years ago. Be careful! Some learners say: “The souq is thought to have built in the 1820s.” That’s not right. We say: “The souq is thought to have been built in the 1820s.” Passive → to have been + past participle. Quick check: what is wrong with “The roofs should have repaired years ago.”? … Think! … It should be “The roofs should have been repaired years ago.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can argue for the best way to protect a heritage site.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Look! The old minaret ___ right now.","options":["is repairing","has repaired","is being repaired","is repaired"],"answer":"is being repaired","explanation":"Continuous passive: is / was being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول المستمر."},{"q":"Since 2015, more than fifty houses in the old town ___.","options":["are restoring","have restored","have been restored","had restored"],"answer":"have been restored","explanation":"Perfect passive: has / had been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المجهول التام."},{"q":"Ancient artifacts ___ with gloves.","options":["must be handled","must handle","must be handling","must have handle"],"answer":"must be handled","explanation":"Modal passive (must be / should have been).","explanation_ar":"المجهول مع الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"The mud walls ___ before the rainy season.","options":["should been repaired","should have repaired","should be repaired yesterday","should have been repaired"],"answer":"should have been repaired","explanation":"Modal passive (must be / should have been).","explanation_ar":"المجهول مع الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"Nobody likes ___ in front of visitors.","options":["been criticized","being criticized","to criticizing","criticizing"],"answer":"being criticized","explanation":"Passive gerund (being / having been + past participle).","explanation_ar":"المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"The old mosque in the village center ______ by local families for more than three hundred years, and it is still in excellent condition.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["has been looked after","has been looked","has looking after","has looked after"],"answer":"has been looked after","explanation":"Prepositional or two-object verbs in the passive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المركبة وذات المفعولين."},{"q":"___ that the inscriptions were written by travelers.","options":["They were once believed","It was once believing","It was once believed","It once believed"],"answer":"It was once believed","explanation":"It was believed / thought / said that… (past belief).","explanation_ar":"It was believed that."},{"q":"The palace is thought ___ in only five years.","options":["to build","building","to have been built","to have built"],"answer":"to have been built","explanation":"Subject + is thought + to have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"The wealthy trader is said ___ a school for poor children in 1890.","options":["to have been founded","founding it","to be founded","to have founded"],"answer":"to have founded","explanation":"Active (to have done) or passive (to have been done)?","explanation_ar":"المعلوم أم المجهول؟"},{"q":"The workers ___ the old palace, keeping its original design and materials.","options":["vandalized","restored","excavated","renovated with steel"],"answer":"restored","explanation":"Choose between related verbs (preserve / restore / renovate).","explanation_ar":"الفروق الدقيقة."},{"q":"The museum shop sells ___ of ancient coins, not the real ones.","options":["replicas","artifacts","inscriptions","landmarks"],"answer":"replicas","explanation":"Heritage word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Folk tales and traditional songs are part of our ___ heritage.","options":["dilapidated","renovated","intangible","authentic"],"answer":"intangible","explanation":"Heritage word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Archaeologists ______ the ancient settlement slowly and carefully, using small brushes so that nothing would be damaged.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["renovated","vandalized","demolished","excavated"],"answer":"excavated","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."},{"q":"Without repairs, the old wooden balconies will continue to ___.","options":["safeguard","deteriorate","excavate","inscribe"],"answer":"deteriorate","explanation":"Heritage word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The volunteers cleaned the site, repaired the walls and ___ new signs.","options":["installed","to install","they installed","installing"],"answer":"installed","explanation":"Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"The festival is not only fun but also ___.","options":["education","educational","to educate","it educates"],"answer":"educational","explanation":"Correlative conjunctions with matching structures.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط المزدوجة."},{"q":"","options":["Neither the guide or the visitors could read the ancient inscription.","Neither the guide nor the visitors could read the ancient inscription.","Neither the guide nor could the visitors read the ancient inscription.","Not the guide nor the visitors could read the ancient inscription."],"answer":"Neither the guide nor the visitors could read the ancient inscription.","explanation":"Correlative conjunctions with matching structures.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط المزدوجة."},{"q":"Repairing old manuscripts is harder than ___ new books.","options":["printed","print","to print","printing"],"answer":"printing","explanation":"Parallel comparison.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في المقارنة."},{"q":"The heritage program trains young people to identify damaged buildings, report vandalism and ______ visitors through historic sites.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["guiding","they guide","to guiding","guide"],"answer":"guide","explanation":"Parallel items in a list.","explanation_ar":"التوازي في القائمة."},{"q":"The restoration of the old fort took four years. ______ the fort now welcomes thousands of visitors every month.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["In contrast,","Today,","However,","For example,"],"answer":"Today,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Historic Jeddah was added to the UNESCO World Heritage List in 2014.\n• Its houses were built from coral stone.\n• Their wooden balconies are called rawashin.\n• The rawashin let in breezes and kept homes cool.\n\nThe student wants to explain how the traditional houses were designed for the hot climate. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Jeddah has a hot climate.","The houses of Historic Jeddah are built from coral stone.","Historic Jeddah was added to the UNESCO World Heritage List in 2014.","Built from coral stone, the houses of Historic Jeddah have wooden balconies called rawashin that let in breezes and keep homes cool."],"answer":"Built from coral stone, the houses of Historic Jeddah have wooden balconies called rawashin that let in breezes and keep homes cool.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"Which sentence breaks the pattern of a parallel list?","options":["The museum displays old coins, pottery and it has manuscripts.","The museum displays and protects old coins.","The museum displays old coins and rare manuscripts.","The museum displays old coins, pottery and manuscripts."],"answer":"The museum displays old coins, pottery and it has manuscripts.","explanation":"Choose the best correction.","explanation_ar":"أفضل تصحيح."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"the old fort is thought to have built in 1800, and it should restored.\"","options":["the old fort is thought to have been built in 1800, and it should be restored.","The old fort is thought to have been built in 1800, and it should restored.","The old fort is thought to have been built in 1800, and it should be restored.","The old fort is thought to have built in 1800, and it should be restored."],"answer":"The old fort is thought to have been built in 1800, and it should be restored.","explanation":"Subject + is thought + to have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"\"The house is said to have been built by a merchant.\" Who built the house?","options":["a merchant","We know nothing.","the house","the people who are speaking"],"answer":"a merchant","explanation":"Active (to have done) or passive (to have been done)?","explanation_ar":"المعلوم أم المجهول؟"}],"theme_ar":"حماية تراثنا","essential_question_ar":"مَن المسؤول عن حماية الماضي، وكيف ينبغي أن يتم ذلك؟","can_do":"I can use advanced passive forms (continuous, perfect, modal, gerund and get-passives), report beliefs about the past with passive reporting structures, use precise conservation vocabulary, and write with parallel structure.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أستخدم صيغ المبني للمجهول المتقدمة (المستمر والتام ومع الأفعال الناقصة والمصدر وget)، وأنقل المعتقدات عن الماضي بتراكيب النقل المبنية للمجهول، وأستخدم مفردات الحفاظ على التراث بدقة، وأكتب بتراكيب متوازية."});
